IMPORT prelude

-- School Education Act 1999 (Western Australia) -- the precompulsory and compulsory education periods (ss 4, 5, 6), compulsory
-- enrolment and how it is satisfied (ss 9, 10, 11), the alternatives in the final two years (ss 11B, 11C, 11D, 11F, 11G, 11H),
-- attendance and when a student is excused (ss 23, 25), the parent's and child's offences and what must happen before a prosecution
-- (ss 38, 39, 40, 41, 42), and the right to enrol at a government school (ss 75, 76, 78, 79).
--
-- Edition: compilation from legislation.wa.gov.au (mrdoc 49345, retrieved 7 September 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49345.txt. The deposit names no compilation number; its compilation table ends with the
-- Education and Care Services National Law Application Act 2026 Pt 6 Div 7 (in force 1 May 2026), the last reprint listed is
-- Reprint 4 as at 19 February 2016, and the deposit carries "(c) State of Western Australia 2026". The uncommenced provisions table
-- lists only the Act's own s 182(3) and s 208.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement au/wa:REQ-0005 (priority 1), raised 8 times by the three Western Australian cradle-to-grave lives
-- (Chloe c010, c011, c078; Jake k010, k011, k024; Daniel d010, d054). The lives ask: is kindergarten compulsory (c010); from which
-- year must a child attend (c011, k010, d010, d054); which school must enrol a child (c078); whose duty is attendance, and what can
-- the Department do before it prosecutes a parent (k011); may a 16-year-old leave school for a pre-apprenticeship (k024). SCOPED to
-- ss 5, 6, 9, 11B, 23, 38-40 and 78, which the lives cite, with the definitions, conditions and exceptions needed to answer them.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the procedure for the information a parent gives on enrolment (ss 15-16), s 11AA (proof of enrolment), s 11E
-- (combinations of courses and the Minister's acknowledgment), s 11I beyond its effect through s 11F, s 24 arrangements beyond a flag,
-- ss 27-31 (public health and religious observance absences), attendance officers' powers (ss 33-37), s 43 onward of Division 5,
-- home education (Division 6, beyond registration as a flag), Parts 3 to 9 except ss 60 and 75-79 (government schools, curriculum,
-- non-government schools, kindergartens, residential colleges, fees and charges). Regulations, the Minister's orders under
-- s 11B(2), Gazette orders under s 60 (intake areas) and school-year orders under s 117 were not retrieved: they are INPUTS.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `School Education Act 1999 (WA) -- compulsory schooling`

§§ `helpers`

-- Dates are written as whole numbers YYYYMMDD (2010-02-01 is 20100201), so later dates are larger numbers.
-- "the year in which the child reaches the age of N years and M months": the child reaches that age M months after the Nth
-- birthday, which falls in the next calendar year when the birth month plus M passes December.
DECLARE Child HAS
    `born year` IS A NUMBER
    `born month` IS A NUMBER
    `born day` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the child` IS A Child, `years` IS A NUMBER, `extra months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year the child reaches` MEANS
    IF `the child`'s `born month` PLUS `extra months` GREATER THAN 12
    THEN `the child`'s `born year` PLUS `years` PLUS 1
    ELSE `the child`'s `born year` PLUS `years`

GIVEN `first date` IS A NUMBER, `second date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the earlier of` MEANS
    IF `first date` AT MOST `second date` THEN `first date` ELSE `second date`

GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first day of` MEANS `the year` TIMES 10000 PLUS 101

GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day of` MEANS `the year` TIMES 10000 PLUS 1231

§§ `5 -- precompulsory education period`

-- s 5: "The precompulsory education period for a child is as follows -- (a) until 31 December 2012 -- (i) from the beginning of the
-- year in which the child reaches the age of 4 years and 6 months; and (ii) until the end of the year in which the child reaches the
-- age of 5 years and 6 months; (b) from 1 January 2013 -- (i) from the beginning of the year in which the child reaches the age of
-- 4 years and 6 months; and (ii) until the end of that year."
-- s 4: "early education period for a child means the period before the child's precompulsory education period".
-- The paragraphs are chosen by the date on which the question is asked (INFERENCE from "until 31 December 2012" / "from 1 January
-- 2013"). Nothing in the Act makes the precompulsory period compulsory: s 9(1) speaks only of "the compulsory education period".
GIVEN `the child` IS A Child
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first year of the precompulsory education period` MEANS `the year the child reaches` `the child` 4 6

GIVEN `the child` IS A Child, `the date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last year of the precompulsory education period` MEANS
    IF `the date` LESS THAN 20130101
    THEN `the year the child reaches` `the child` 5 6
    ELSE `the first year of the precompulsory education period` `the child`

GIVEN `the child` IS A Child, `the date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in the precompulsory education period` IF
        `the date` AT LEAST `the first day of` (`the first year of the precompulsory education period` `the child`)
    AND `the date` AT MOST `the last day of` (`the last year of the precompulsory education period` `the child` `the date`)

§§ `6 -- compulsory education period`

-- s 6(1): "(a) until 31 December 2012 -- (i) from the beginning of the year in which the child reaches the age of 6 years and
-- 6 months; and (ii) until the end of the year in which the child reaches the age of 17; (b) from 1 January 2013 until 31 December
-- 2013 -- (i) from the beginning of the year in which the child reaches the age of 5 years and 6 months; and (ii) until the end of
-- the year in which the child reaches the age of 17; (c) from 1 January 2014 -- (i) from the beginning of the year in which the child
-- reaches the age of 5 years and 6 months; and (ii) until -- (I) the end of the year in which the child reaches the age of 17 years
-- and 6 months; or (II) the child reaches the age of 18, whichever happens first."
-- (2): if the child satisfies the minimum requirements for graduation from secondary school before the end of the period, "this Act
-- applies in respect of the child as if the compulsory education period for the child ended when the requirements were satisfied."
--
-- The Act says nothing of "by 30 June". It counts from the YEAR in which the child reaches 6 years 6 months (to 2012) or 5 years
-- 6 months (from 2013) -- a child born in March reaches 6 years 6 months in September, so that whole calendar year is compulsory.
-- Like s 5, the paragraphs are chosen by the date on which the question is asked (INFERENCE). Under paragraph (c) the period usually
-- ends on the 18th birthday, not at a year's end: 17 years 6 months is reached in the year before the 18th birthday only for a child
-- born in July to December, and then the 18th birthday comes first.
GIVEN `the child` IS A Child, `the date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first year of the compulsory education period` MEANS
    IF `the date` LESS THAN 20130101
    THEN `the year the child reaches` `the child` 6 6
    ELSE `the year the child reaches` `the child` 5 6

GIVEN `the child` IS A Child
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 18th birthday of` MEANS
    (`the child`'s `born year` PLUS 18) TIMES 10000 PLUS `the child`'s `born month` TIMES 100 PLUS `the child`'s `born day`

GIVEN `the child` IS A Child, `the date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day of the compulsory education period` MEANS
    IF `the date` LESS THAN 20140101
    THEN `the last day of` (`the child`'s `born year` PLUS 17)
    ELSE `the earlier of` (`the last day of` (`the year the child reaches` `the child` 17 6)) (`the 18th birthday of` `the child`)

-- s 6(2) is taken as a flag: the child had met the graduation requirements by the date asked about.
GIVEN `the child` IS A Child, `the date` IS A NUMBER, `has met the graduation requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in the compulsory education period` IF
        `the date` AT LEAST `the first day of` (`the first year of the compulsory education period` `the child` `the date`)
    AND `the date` AT MOST `the last day of the compulsory education period` `the child` `the date`
    AND (NOT `has met the graduation requirements`)

-- s 4: "final years of compulsory education for a child means the final 2 years of the compulsory education period for the child".
-- Taken here (INFERENCE) as the days after the date two years before the period's last day (YYYYMMDD minus 20000), up to and
-- including that last day. A 29 February birthday is not handled.
GIVEN `the child` IS A Child, `the date` IS A NUMBER, `has met the graduation requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in the final years of compulsory education` IF
        `in the compulsory education period` `the child` `the date` `has met the graduation requirements`
    AND `the date` GREATER THAN `the last day of the compulsory education period` `the child` `the date` MINUS 20000

§§ `4 -- parent`

-- s 4: "parent, in relation to a child, means a person who at law has responsibility -- (a) for the longterm care, welfare and
-- development of the child; or (b) for the day to day care, welfare and development of the child, except in sections 9(2), 10(1)(b),
-- 25, 27, 38(1) and Division 6 of Part 2 where it has only the meaning given by paragraph (b)".
-- So a parent who has only long-term responsibility is not the "parent" who commits the s 9(2) or s 38(1) offence.
GIVEN `long-term responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN, `day-to-day responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a parent in the general sense` IF `long-term responsibility` OR `day-to-day responsibility`

GIVEN `long-term responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN, `day-to-day responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a parent for sections 9(2) and 38(1)` IF `day-to-day responsibility`

§§ `9, 10, 11, 11F, 11H -- compulsory enrolment`

-- s 9(1): "A child is to be enrolled in an educational programme for each year of the compulsory education period for that child."
-- (1a): subject to ss 11F(2) and 11H(5) and (6). (2): "A parent of a child must ensure that subsection (1) is complied with. Penalty:
-- a fine of $2 500." (3): no prosecution "unless the chief executive officer has given a certificate to the effect that reasonably
-- practicable steps have been taken to secure compliance".
-- s 10(1): the duty is satisfied by "(a) the enrolment of the child at a school; or (b) the registration under section 48 of a
-- parent as the child's home educator and the continuation in effect of that registration."
-- s 11(2): s 9(1) "does not apply to a child who is exempted by the Minister ... if the conditions of the exemption are being
-- complied with". s 11F(2): "While a notice is in force, section 9(1) does not apply". s 11H(5): the same for a notice of full-time
-- employment with the Minister's approval.
DECLARE Enrolment HAS
    `enrolled at a school` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a parent is registered as home educator` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exempt by the Minister and complying with the conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a section 11D notice is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a section 11H notice of full-time employment is in force` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the child` IS A Child, `the date` IS A NUMBER, `has met the graduation requirements` IS A BOOLEAN, `the enrolment` IS AN Enrolment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 9(1) applies` IF
        `in the compulsory education period` `the child` `the date` `has met the graduation requirements`
    AND (NOT `the enrolment`'s `exempt by the Minister and complying with the conditions`)
    AND (NOT `the enrolment`'s `a section 11D notice is in force`)
    AND (NOT `the enrolment`'s `a section 11H notice of full-time employment is in force`)

GIVEN `the enrolment` IS AN Enrolment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 10 is satisfied` IF
    `the enrolment`'s `enrolled at a school` OR `the enrolment`'s `a parent is registered as home educator`

GIVEN `the child` IS A Child, `the date` IS A NUMBER, `has met the graduation requirements` IS A BOOLEAN, `the enrolment` IS AN Enrolment,
      `day-to-day responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the parent is in breach of section 9(2)` IF
        `section 9(1) applies` `the child` `the date` `has met the graduation requirements` `the enrolment`
    AND (NOT `section 10 is satisfied` `the enrolment`)
    AND `a parent for sections 9(2) and 38(1)` FALSE `day-to-day responsibility`

`the maximum fine under section 9(2)` MEANS 2500

§§ `11B, 11C, 11D, 11G -- options other than school in the final two years`

-- s 11B(1): "In the final years of compulsory education a child may, despite section 9(1), participate in one or more of the
-- following options -- (a) undertaking -- (i) a course of study provided by a university ...; or (ii) a higher education course
-- registered under section 23 of the Higher Education Act 2004; or (b) undertaking an approved VET course within the meaning given to
-- that term by the Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 section 5(1); or (c) being an apprentice; or (d) being employed under a
-- contract of employment ... but subject to approval being in force under section 11G; or (e) undertaking a course prescribed under
-- subsection (2)."
-- s 11C(1): participation "must be on a fulltime basis". s 11D(1): a parent "must give notice to the Minister as soon as is
-- practicable after the arrangements are made"; (7) the notice "comes into force when it is given". s 11G(1): no employment under
-- 11B(1)(d) "unless the approval of the Minister has been obtained". s 11H(1): notice of the employment. s 11F(2): while the notice
-- is in force, s 9(1) does not apply.
-- Whether a TAFE pre-apprenticeship is an "approved VET course" is a question under the VET Act 1996, not this Act: INPUT.
DECLARE Option IS ONE OF
    `a university course`
    `a registered higher education course`
    `an approved VET course`
    `an apprenticeship`
    `employment with the Minister's approval`
    `employment without the Minister's approval`
    `a course prescribed by the Minister's order`
    `no course, training or employment`

GIVEN `the option` IS AN Option
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the option is listed in section 11B(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the option`
    WHEN `employment without the Minister's approval` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `no course, training or employment` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the child` IS A Child, `the date` IS A NUMBER, `the option` IS AN Option, `full-time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the child may take the option instead of school` IF
        `in the final years of compulsory education` `the child` `the date` FALSE
    AND `the option is listed in section 11B(1)` `the option`
    AND `full-time`

-- With the option taken and the parent's notice given (s 11D, or s 11H for employment), s 9(1) stops applying (ss 11F(2), 11H(5)).
GIVEN `the child` IS A Child, `the date` IS A NUMBER, `the option` IS AN Option, `full-time` IS A BOOLEAN, `the parent gave notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the child may leave school for the option` IF
        `the child may take the option instead of school` `the child` `the date` `the option` `full-time`
    AND `the parent gave notice`

§§ `23, 25 -- attendance, and when a student is excused`

-- s 23(1): "A student must, for every year of the student's compulsory education period, on the days on which the school is open for
-- instruction -- (a) either -- (i) attend the school at which the student is enrolled; or (ii) otherwise participate in an educational
-- programme of the school ... as required by the principal; or (b) comply with an arrangement under section 24." (2): subject to
-- ss 25, 27 and 30.
-- s 25(2): excused "(a) if the student is prevented from attending ... by -- (i) temporary physical or mental incapacity; or (ii) any
-- other reasonable cause; and (b) if a responsible person has notified the principal of the cause ... (i) as soon as is practicable;
-- and (ii) in any case within 3 school days of the day on which the nonattendance started; and (c) where ... the incapacity of the
-- student is given as the cause, if the responsible person provides the principal with a certificate in support from a registered
-- medical practitioner if requested to do so by the principal." (4): excused also where a parent has applied or intends to apply to
-- be registered as home educator and notified the principal in writing within 3 school days.
DECLARE Absence HAS
    `prevented by temporary incapacity or other reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the cause was notified within 3 school days` IS A BOOLEAN
    `incapacity was the cause given` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the principal asked for a medical certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a medical certificate was provided` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a home-education application was notified in writing within 3 school days` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the absence` IS AN Absence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the absence is excused under section 25` IF
        (    `the absence`'s `prevented by temporary incapacity or other reasonable cause`
         AND `the absence`'s `the cause was notified within 3 school days`
         AND (    (NOT `the absence`'s `incapacity was the cause given`)
              OR  (NOT `the absence`'s `the principal asked for a medical certificate`)
              OR  `the absence`'s `a medical certificate was provided`))
    OR  `the absence`'s `a home-education application was notified in writing within 3 school days`

-- s 32: "absentee student means a child of compulsory school age who is in breach of section 23". The day is taken to be one on
-- which the school was open for instruction and the student neither attended nor otherwise participated as the principal required.
GIVEN `the child` IS A Child, `the date` IS A NUMBER, `enrolled` IS A BOOLEAN, `the absence` IS AN Absence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the student is in breach of section 23` IF
        `in the compulsory education period` `the child` `the date` FALSE
    AND `enrolled`
    AND (NOT `the absence is excused under section 25` `the absence`)

§§ `38 -- the offences`

-- s 38(1): "A parent of a child of compulsory school age who is enrolled at a school must ensure that section 23 is complied with by
-- the child. Penalty: a fine of $1 000." (2): "A child of compulsory school age who is enrolled at a school must comply with section
-- 23. Penalty: a fine of $10." For s 38(1) "parent" has only its day-to-day meaning (s 4).
GIVEN `the child` IS A Child, `the date` IS A NUMBER, `the absence` IS AN Absence, `day-to-day responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the parent is in breach of section 38(1)` IF
        `the student is in breach of section 23` `the child` `the date` TRUE `the absence`
    AND `a parent for sections 9(2) and 38(1)` FALSE `day-to-day responsibility`

`the maximum fine under section 38(1)` MEANS 1000
`the maximum fine under section 38(2)` MEANS 10

§§ `39, 40 -- Attendance Panels`

-- s 40(1): "Where a child of compulsory school age enrolled at a school has been persistently in breach of section 23, the child's
-- case may be referred to an Attendance Panel by -- (a) the principal of the school; or (b) an attendance officer; or (c) the chief
-- executive officer". (2): the Panel "is to -- (a) inquire into the reasons for the child's failure ... including the social,
-- cultural, lingual, economic or geographic factors, or learning difficulties ...; and (b) give such advice and assistance to the
-- child and to his or her parents as it thinks fit." (3A): it "may advise that a responsible parenting agreement under the Children
-- and Community Services Act 2004 be entered into". (3): the chairperson may by notice "request the attendance of a child and his or
-- her parents". (5): a written report. s 39(1): at least 3 persons; (3) at least one "a parent or community representative".
-- The Panel advises, assists, requests and reports. Nothing in ss 39-40 lets it fine, order or prosecute; the responsible parenting
-- agreement is made under another Act.
DECLARE Referrer IS ONE OF
    `the principal of the school`
    `an attendance officer`
    `the chief executive officer`
    `a class teacher who is not an attendance officer`
    `a neighbour`

GIVEN `the referrer` IS A Referrer, `persistently in breach` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the referrer may refer the case to an Attendance Panel` IF
        `persistently in breach`
    AND CONSIDER `the referrer`
        WHEN `the principal of the school` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an attendance officer` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the chief executive officer` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE PanelStep IS ONE OF
    `inquire into the reasons for the absences`
    `give advice and assistance to the child and parents`
    `advise a responsible parenting agreement`
    `request the child and parents to attend`
    `prepare a written report`
    `fine the parent`
    `order the child to attend school`
    `commence a prosecution`

GIVEN `the step` IS A PanelStep
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Panel may take the step` IF
    CONSIDER `the step`
    WHEN `fine the parent` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `order the child to attend school` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `commence a prosecution` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 39(1), (3): a Panel of at least 3, with at least one parent or community representative.
GIVEN `members` IS A NUMBER, `parent or community representatives` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Panel is properly constituted` IF
    `members` AT LEAST 3 AND `parent or community representatives` AT LEAST 1

§§ `41, 42 -- before a parent is prosecuted under section 38`

-- s 42(1): no prosecution under s 38(1) or (2) "unless a certificate has been given that -- (a) reasonably practicable steps have
-- been taken to secure compliance with section 23 by the child; but (b) breaches of the section have continued." (2): given by the
-- Attendance Panel or the chief executive officer.
-- s 41(1): where the case was referred to a Panel and the Panel gave advice or offered assistance, "a prosecution for an offence
-- against section 38 is not to be commenced unless there has been failure to follow the advice or accept the assistance."
GIVEN `a section 42 certificate was given` IS A BOOLEAN, `a Panel gave advice or offered assistance` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the advice was not followed or the assistance not accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 38 prosecution may be commenced` IF
        `a section 42 certificate was given`
    AND (    (NOT `a Panel gave advice or offered assistance`)
         OR  `the advice was not followed or the assistance not accepted`)

§§ `75, 76, 78, 79 -- which government school must enrol the child`

-- s 76(1): "A child is not entitled to be enrolled at a government school unless -- (a) the usual place of residence of the child is
-- in the State; and (b) the child is entitled to reside permanently in Australia." (2): or meets criteria prescribed by regulations.
-- s 78(1): "A child of compulsory school age is entitled to be enrolled at a localintake school if -- (a) his or her usual place of
-- residence is in the intake area for that school; and (b) an appropriate educational programme is available for the child at that
-- school." (2): from outside the intake area only if there is an appropriate programme AND classroom accommodation AND any
-- regulation criteria are met. s 79(1): the same three conditions at a school that is not local-intake; (2) priority to "the child
-- who lives nearest the school".
-- s 75(1): "The principal of a government school is to enrol a child at the school if -- (a) an application is duly made under
-- section 74; and (b) the child is entitled under this Division to be enrolled at the school." (2): not if the child is already
-- enrolled at a school and the attendance applied for is likely to be less than 4 weeks.
-- Intake areas are set by the chief executive officer's order in the Gazette (s 60): INPUT. Classroom accommodation is not a
-- condition for a child living in the intake area.
DECLARE Applicant HAS
    `usually resides in the State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `entitled to reside permanently in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `meets the regulations' criteria for other children` IS A BOOLEAN
    `of compulsory school age` IS A BOOLEAN
    `usually resides in the intake area` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an appropriate programme is available` IS A BOOLEAN
    `classroom accommodation is available` IS A BOOLEAN
    `other prescribed criteria are met` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 76 is satisfied` IF
        (`the applicant`'s `usually resides in the State` AND `the applicant`'s `entitled to reside permanently in Australia`)
    OR  `the applicant`'s `meets the regulations' criteria for other children`

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to enrol at the local-intake school` IF
        `section 76 is satisfied` `the applicant`
    AND `the applicant`'s `of compulsory school age`
    AND (    (`the applicant`'s `usually resides in the intake area` AND `the applicant`'s `an appropriate programme is available`)
         OR  (    `the applicant`'s `an appropriate programme is available`
              AND `the applicant`'s `classroom accommodation is available`
              AND `the applicant`'s `other prescribed criteria are met`))

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant, `application duly made` IS A BOOLEAN, `already enrolled and staying under 4 weeks` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the principal of the local-intake school must enrol the child` IF
        `application duly made`
    AND `entitled to enrol at the local-intake school` `the applicant`
    AND (NOT `already enrolled and staying under 4 weeks`)
